kunzite: op 4, the container-path lookup, always answers (the containers kit's implementation,
patch 1003 v2; design from 1002's boot-#62 dump). Boot #62 showed op 4 is called by everyone —
cfprefsd alone 21,368 times in ten minutes, retrying on the ENOENT — and almost no process here
carries CFFIXED_USER_HOME, so 0936's environment answer almost always fell to 0970's ENOENT.
topaz_sandbox_container.c now captures the target's uid while the proc is held and falls back
to its home (/private/var/root for uid 0, /private/var/mobile otherwise) at every exit that
used to return ENOENT: no environment, no map, a failed stack read, or no CFFIXED_USER_HOME.
The environment answer, when the variable is there, is unchanged; a dead pid still gets ESRCH.
v1 of this patch defined the answer as a strong symbol in sweet_amfi.c and CI's link failed:
0936's definition in topaz_sandbox_container.o already is the strong one the weak stand-in in
sweet_amfi.c defers to. sweet_amfi.c keeps only the other change: 1002's argument dump now
prints only with sweet_sbx_dump=1 in the boot-args, so the console storm goes with the retry
storm.

